    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/text",
      "value": "Twice differentiating u·u=1 in time gives 2|u_t|²+2u·u_tt=0. For each coordinate j0=1,...,n, twice differentiating in x_j similarly gives 2|∂_{x_j0}u|²+2u·∂_{x_jx_j0}u=0. Thus u·u_tt=−|u_t|² and u·∂_{x_jx_j0}u=−|∂_{x_j0}u|². Dot the normality equation for a with u and use |u|²=1. Finite distributivity and the definition of Δ_xu give a=u·(u_tt−Δ_xu)=Σ_{j=1}^n|∂_{x_j0}u|²−|u_t|². The same calculation applies to every scalar satisfying that pointwise equation."
    },
